## Relationships

### Semantic
- [CXC-HKR] RELATED_TO [CXC-DSDV] — sibling delivery endpoints on the one decision-ops surface
- [CXC-HKR-MCP] RELATED_TO [CXC-DSDV-MCP] — the same validate/publish/correlate contract
- [CXC-HKR-MCP] RELATED_TO [CXC-DSDV-REGISTER] — the same both-surfaces registration invariant
- [CXC-HKR-LABEL-GATE] DEPENDS_ON [CXC-HKR-RENDER-NOT-ACCEPT] — the gate is only possible because the endpoint owns the rasterizer
- [CXC-HKR-LABEL-DETECTOR] PART_OF [CXC-HKR-LABEL-GATE]
- [CXC-HKR-LABEL-DETECTOR] CONVERGES_TO [CXC-BOARD-HW-VALUE-CODEC-FORK] — the SAME one-table defect, third instance: two agents, hours apart on one day, each wrote the label-survival check because neither could see the other. Collapsed onto one primitive the same way the message-type table and the value codec were.
- [CXC-HKR-FAULT-INJECTOR] PART_OF [CXC-HKR-LABEL-GATE]
- [CXC-HKR-CROSSING-GATE] DEPENDS_ON [CXC-HKR-RENDER-NOT-ACCEPT] — the endpoint can only gate on the crossing verdict because it OWNS the render; an accepted image carries no report
- [CXC-HKR-HOP-SURVIVAL] PART_OF [CXC-HKR-CROSSING-GATE] — the same lie, one layer down: the planner refused to draw the bridge, or the rasterizer lost it
- [CXC-HKR-HOP-SURVIVAL] DEPENDS_ON [CXC-HKR-LABEL-DETECTOR] — one differential (`_ink_vs_reference`), two features; the second check rides the named shared surface instead of forking it
- [CXC-HKR-HOP-FAULT-INJECTOR] PART_OF [CXC-HKR-HOP-SURVIVAL]
- [CXC-HKR-HOP-FAULT-INJECTOR] RELATED_TO [CXC-HKR-FAULT-INJECTOR] — the same discipline, one real fault and one synthesised, because the failure mode a gate cannot reproduce is the one it stops catching
- [CXC-HKR-SELFTEST-ROOT] PART_OF [CXC-HKR-LABEL-GATE] — the gate is only as trustworthy as the instrument that reports on it; a harness measuring another tree reported this gate broken while it was firing correctly
- [CXC-HKR-SELFTEST-ROOT] RELATED_TO [CXC-DSDV-MCP] — the same defect, two instances: `dsd_review._selftest` carried the identical relative-fixture split-brain and is fixed in the same change. One `own_checkout_root()`, both callers — reuse by reference, not a second copy ([DX-NARROW-WAIST])
- [CXC-HKR-DO-NOT-SCHEMA] RELATED_TO [CXC-HKR-NEGATIVE-SPACE] — the proposed schema behind the carriage
